From b53cbfa18368137a8b4a528b398816ce443ce272 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:26:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 145/638] content: stop AROS renderer scheduler before destroy
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: Checkpoint 0146 proved the AROS in-process renderer can be destroyed, but RenderThreadImpl::ShouldBeDestroyed returned true without supplying Blink scheduler shutdown. MainThreadSchedulerImpl therefore reached its destructor with was_shutdown_ false and deliberately trapped after the page screenshot completed.

FIX_REASON: ChildProcess already invokes RenderThreadImpl::Shutdown before ShouldBeDestroyed and ownership reset. Shut down the owned WebThreadScheduler from that lifecycle hook so it drops queued work and clears scheduler state before member destruction.

SCOPE: AROS single-process renderer shutdown only; multi-process termination and every other platform retain upstream behavior.

VALIDATION: render_thread_impl.o rebuilt successfully; artifact 51 captures the exact was_shutdown_ fatal and confirms screenshot output completed first.

RISK: medium; scheduler shutdown is final and intentionally drops pending Blink work, but runs only after browser teardown has initiated renderer shutdown.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc b/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
index 4cb27130ee..8359259fff 100644
--- a/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
+++ b/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
@@ -668,6 +668,13 @@ void RenderThreadImpl::Shutdown() {
 
   blink::LogStatsDuringShutdown();
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
+  if (IsSingleProcess() && main_thread_scheduler_) {
+    LOG(INFO) << "[Chromium:shutdown] stopping AROS renderer scheduler";
+    main_thread_scheduler_->Shutdown();
+  }
+#endif
+
   // In a single-process mode, we cannot call _exit(0) in Shutdown() because
   // it will exit the process before the browser side is ready to exit.
   if (!IsSingleProcess())
